          >
        </nav>
        <h1>Appendix N</h1>
        <p class="dek">Procedural 0E campaigns as a turn-based PC roguelike. Early access.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-body">
        <p>
          Appendix N runs the procedures of old-school tabletop play as one long single-player
          campaign. You roll up a company, outfit it in town, walk out the gate and strike across a
          generated hexcrawl, chasing rumors and commissions down into generated dungeons.
        </p>
        <p>
          The first ruleset is 0E, written into the game as data, so every roll, table and procedure
          comes from the loaded rules. Travel costs watches. Food, light, weather and the weight you
          carry all count. When something finds you, the reaction roll sets the tone: parley, slip
          away, hire them, or fight.
        </p>
        <p>
          Persistent worlds with save and continue. Dead and retired characters go into the
          Chronicle. One persistent world, short commands, and a company that has to earn its next
          watch.
        </p>
      </div>

